{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`985f` added a session-wide git-identity scrub to `tests/conftest.py`. On a machine whose\ngit identity is supplied *only* by the harness-injected command-scope config, that scrub\nleaves `repo_root` with no resolvable `user.email`, and 5 `test_doctor.py` tests that drive\n`doctor repair` abort. This is a regression introduced by `985f`, live on `main`.\n\n## Root cause — established by measurement, not inference\n\nThree facts, each verified directly:\n\n1. **The identity the repair reads comes from `repo_root`, not the tracker.**\n   `owned_repair_pause` (`src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py:117`) calls\n   `identity._git_email(root)` where `root = config.repo_root(repo_root)`.\n   `_git_email` (`src/rebar/_commands/identity.py:86-102`) shells `git config user.email`\n   with `cwd=root`.\n\n2. **In this checkout, `repo_root` identity is ambient-only.**\n   ```\n   git config --local  user.email   -> (empty)\n   git config --global user.email   -> (empty)\n   GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=8\n   git config user.email            -> joeoakhart@navapbc.com\n   ```\n   Local and global are both unset. The resolved value comes solely from the\n   harness-injected `GIT_CONFIG_*` command-scope variables — exactly what\n   `scrub_ambient_git_config` removes.\n\n3. **The failing tests configure identity on a DIFFERENT repo.**\n   `_git_backed` (`tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py:437-448`) runs\n   `git config user.email t@example.invalid` against the **tmp tracker**. The 5 failing\n   tests redirect only `tracker_dir` (lines 518, 567, 655, 697, 733) and never redirect\n   `repo_root`. So the identity they establish is invisible to the check, which reads the\n   real checkout.\n\n**The 5 tests that redirect `tracker_dir` are exactly the 5 that fail.** That\ncorrespondence is the confirmation.\n\nThis also explains why CI is green: a runner with a global `user.email` satisfies the\n`repo_root` lookup regardless of the scrub. The defect only manifests where identity is\nambient-only.\n\n### Bisect\n\n| Commit | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `bed0718fba9` (parent) | 22 passed, **0 failures** |\n| `ddb1d953812` (`985f` merged) | **5 failures** |\n\nAll 5 reduce to `RepairPauseError: doctor repair requires a configured git user.email`.\nTwo surface as downstream `JSONDecodeError` (the command aborted, emitting no JSON); one as\na regex-mismatch assertion on that same message.\n\n## Superseded framing\n\nAn earlier comment on this ticket said these failures were \"re-exposed\" by reverting an\nout-of-scope `doctor.py` change. That is wrong and is retained only as history.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe scrub is correct and stays. `_repair_pause.py` is correct and stays. The defect is that\nthese tests depend on an ambient `repo_root` identity they never established.\n\nAdd a helper in `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py`, beside `scrub_ambient_git_config`, that\n**establishes a deliberate identity on a caller-supplied repo path** by running\n`git config user.email` / `user.name` **in that repo** (repo-local config on disk, scoped\nto the tmp repo that the test already owns and `tmp_path` already cleans up).\n\n**It must not mutate `os.environ` and must not set global config.** That constraint is the\npoint: the session-wide `os.environ` mutation is the failure mode under repair here, and\nre-introducing it in the fix would strip the isolation the scrub bought for every other\nidentity test. Writing repo-local config into a `tmp_path` repo has a lifecycle bounded by\nthe fixture, needs no create/retire protocol, and cannot leak into another test.\n\nThen make the 5 tests establish identity on the `repo_root` the repair actually reads —\neither by pointing `repo_root` at the tmp tracker (which `_git_backed` already configures)\nor by configuring the root they inherit. The choice between those two is an implementation\ndecision for the executor; both satisfy the ACs, and the second is preferred if redirecting\n`repo_root` turns out to change what else the command under test resolves.\n\n### Rejected\n\n- **Weakening or removing the scrub.** It is what fixed the identity nodeids in `985f`.\n  Trading those for these 5 is a net regression.\n- **Reinstating `985f`'s `doctor.py` change.** It masked the abort rather than fixing it,\n  and it was out of scope for `985f`.\n- **Setting a global `user.email` in the harness.** Mutates developer machine state outside\n  the repo and is not portable across environments or CI providers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] **Reproduce first.** With the scrub active, the 5 doctor nodeids fail with\n  `RepairPauseError: doctor repair requires a configured git user.email`. Verified by\n  running `python -m pytest tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py -p no:randomly -q` before any\n  code change and recording the verbatim failure output on this ticket.\n- [ ] **After the fix, all 5 pass.** Verified by `python -m pytest\n  tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py -p no:randomly -q` reporting 0 failures, full output\n  recorded. Enumerate the exact 5 nodeids from the AC1 reproduction rather than transcribing\n  them from this description, so the list is measured.\n- [ ] **The scrub is not weakened.** The diff must not modify `tests/conftest.py:168` or the\n  body of `scrub_ambient_git_config`. Verified by `python -m pytest\n  tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py\n  tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py\n  tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_signing_9e76.py -p no:randomly -q` reporting 0\n  failures. That is the complete identity-test oracle — no need to consult `985f`.\n- [ ] **The new helper does not mutate `os.environ`.** Verified by a test asserting\n  `os.environ` is unchanged across a helper call, and by quoting the helper body in a ticket\n  comment to show it writes repo-local git config to a caller-supplied path and never sets\n  global config.\n- [ ] **The same latent dependency is searched for elsewhere.** Verified by reporting every\n  other test that reaches `identity._git_email` against an un-redirected `repo_root`, with\n  the search method stated. Fix any found failing under this ticket; if none, record that the\n  result was empty.\n- [ ] **`make verify` is green.** Verified by running `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make\n  verify` and recording the exit code, with any residual failures attributed to the existing\n  pandoc (`dc28`/`9119`) or sandbox (`0eba`/`985f`) classes and proven pre-existing on the\n  same base.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe proving command for the defect itself is:\n\n```\npython -m pytest tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py -p no:randomly -q\n```\n\nIt must go from 5 failures to 0. The non-regression oracle for the scrub is the four-file\nselection named in AC3, which must stay at 0 failures throughout. `make verify` is the\nfinal check; its known residual classes are enumerated in AC6 and must be shown to reproduce\non the same base without this change before any of them is dismissed."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789712917266852001,"uuid":"5c414f24-eb5e-44fa-8199-cc6a442d8556"}